# partial-concepts-name-collision root
library "Pol".

// A decision-bearing library "Pol" carrying a concept-level `code is`. The
// decision disqualifies the FULL 3-way split, but the `code is` triggers the
// PARTIAL split: emit registers BOTH "Pol" (root) AND the generated "Pol
// Concepts" sibling. A separate REAL library "Pol Concepts" (pol-concepts.crl)
// is pulled into the closure via the qualified ref below, so the generated
// "Pol Concepts" name collides with the real one → kind layered-name-collision.

concept "Adult Patient":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `adult-18-or-older`.

// `From Sibling` aliases the cross-library `Pol Concepts` boolean, which forces the
// `include PolConcepts` on the Inferred layer this fixture asserts.
concept "From Sibling":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as "Pol Concepts"."Sibling Concept".

activity "Refer to GI":
- request CPGServiceRequest.

decision "Triage":
- when "Adult Patient" then recommend activity "Refer to GI".
